<div class="space-y-12">
    <div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Redis Protocol</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-slate-400">The Redis wire protocol on port 6379 &mdash; RESP2 and RESP3, 253 commands, ACL, TLS, transactions, scripting and pub/sub</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Connection -->
    <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-500/10 to-transparent border border-white/10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Connection</h2>
        <div class="font-mono text-sm">
            <div class="text-slate-500"># Connect with redis-cli (default port 6379)</div>
            <div class="text-emerald-400">redis-cli -p 6379</div>
            <div class="text-slate-500 mt-3"># With a password (requirepass, or an ACL user)</div>
            <div class="text-emerald-400">redis-cli -p 6379 --user alice --pass "$PASSWORD"</div>
            <div class="text-slate-500 mt-3"># Over TLS (server started with --tls-cert/--tls-key)</div>
            <div class="text-emerald-400">redis-cli -p 6379 --tls --cacert ca.pem</div>
            <div class="text-slate-500 mt-3"># Any Redis client library works: redis-py, ioredis, go-redis, Jedis, Lettuce, redis-rs …</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Protocol Format -->
    <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Protocol Format</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-400 mb-4">SoliKV speaks RESP, the wire format of Redis. Connections start in RESP2; <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">HELLO 3</code> switches a connection to RESP3, where replies carry their type (maps, sets, doubles, booleans, null) and pub/sub messages arrive as push frames on the same connection. Array and inline commands are both accepted; commands may be pipelined.</p>
        <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-white/10 p-6">
            <pre class="text-sm font-mono text-slate-300 overflow-x-auto">
Array format:    *3\r\n$3\r\nSET\r\n$3\r\nfoo\r\n$3\r\nbar\r\n
Inline format:   SET foo bar\r\n

RESP2 replies:
  Simple string:  +OK\r\n
  Error:          -ERR message\r\n
  Integer:        :42\r\n
  Bulk string:    $3\r\nbar\r\n
  Null:           $-1\r\n
  Array:          *2\r\n$3\r\nfoo\r\n$3\r\nbar\r\n

RESP3 adds (after HELLO 3):
  Null:           _\r\n
  Double:         ,3.14\r\n
  Boolean:        #t\r\n
  Map:            %1\r\n$4\r\nname\r\n$5\r\nAlice\r\n
  Set:            ~2\r\n...
  Push:           >3\r\n$7\r\nmessage\r\n...</pre>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Command Summary -->
    <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-indigo-500/10 border border-indigo-500/30">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-5 gap-4 text-center">
            <div>
                <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-indigo-400">253</div>
                <div class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1">commands</div>
            </div>
            <div>
                <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-emerald-400">RESP3</div>
                <div class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1">and RESP2</div>
            </div>
            <div>
                <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-purple-400">16</div>
                <div class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1">databases</div>
            </div>
            <div>
                <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-cyan-400">WATCH</div>
                <div class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1">transactions</div>
            </div>
            <div>
                <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-pink-400">ACL</div>
                <div class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1">users &amp; TLS</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Families -->
    <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Commands by family</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-400 mb-4">Every command in SoliKV's command table, as <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">COMMAND</code> reports it. Syntax and examples are in the <a href="/docs/commands" class="text-indigo-400 hover:text-white">command reference</a>.</p>
