    <!-- Semantics -->
    <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Semantics worth knowing</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-sm">
            <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
                <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Shards and multi-key commands</h3>
                <p class="text-slate-400">A node splits its keys over <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">--shards</code> shards (one per core by default) by Redis Cluster slot, so <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">{hash tags}</code> keep keys together. Commands spanning shards (<code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">RENAME</code>, <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">SMOVE</code>, <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">MSET</code>, <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">ZUNIONSTORE</code> …) lock every shard involved, so they behave as on a single-threaded server.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
                <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Transactions and scripts</h3>
                <p class="text-slate-400"><code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">MULTI</code>/<code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">EXEC</code> and scripts run atomically. <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">WATCH</code> aborts an <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">EXEC</code> when a watched key changed (writes, expiry, flushes). A queued command with a wrong name or argument count aborts the transaction with <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">EXECABORT</code>.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
                <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Lua</h3>
                <p class="text-slate-400">Lua 5.1, as in Redis, with <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">cjson</code>, <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">cmsgpack</code>, <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">bit</code> and <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">struct</code>. Globals are read-only; a script running longer than <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">--busy-reply-threshold</code> (5 s) makes other clients get <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">-BUSY</code> until it ends or <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">SCRIPT KILL</code>.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
                <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Blocking commands</h3>
                <p class="text-slate-400"><code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">BLPOP</code>, <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">BLMOVE</code>, <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">BZPOPMIN</code>, <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">XREAD BLOCK</code> … serve waiting clients first come, first served; inside <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">MULTI</code> or a script they do not block, as in Redis. <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">CLIENT UNBLOCK</code> releases a client.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Examples -->
    <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Examples</h2>
        <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-white/10 overflow-hidden">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 bg-white/5 border-b border-white/5">
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-mono">redis-cli -p 6379</span>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 font-mono text-sm space-y-1">
                <div class="text-slate-500"># Strings with expiry</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">127.0.0.1:6379&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">SET user:1 Alice EX 3600</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div class="text-slate-500 mt-3"># A job queue with a blocking pop</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">127.0.0.1:6379&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">RPUSH queue job1 job2</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 2</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">127.0.0.1:6379&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">BLMOVE queue processing LEFT RIGHT 5</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">"job1"</div>
                <div class="text-slate-500 mt-3"># Sorted set by score</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">127.0.0.1:6379&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZADD leaderboard 100 alice 200 bob 150 charlie</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">(integer) 3</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">127.0.0.1:6379&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">ZRANGE leaderboard (100 +inf BYSCORE LIMIT 0 10</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) "charlie"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2) "bob"</div>
                <div class="text-slate-500 mt-3"># Optimistic transaction</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">127.0.0.1:6379&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">WATCH balance</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">127.0.0.1:6379&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">MULTI</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">OK</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">127.0.0.1:6379(TX)&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">INCRBY balance -10</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">QUEUED</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">127.0.0.1:6379(TX)&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">EXEC</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1) (integer) -10</div>
                <div class="text-slate-500 mt-3"># Switch the connection to RESP3</div>
                <div><span class="text-slate-500">127.0.0.1:6379&gt;</span> <span class="text-emerald-400">HELLO 3</span></div>
                <div class="text-white">1# "server" =&gt; "redis"</div>
                <div class="text-white">2# "version" =&gt; "7.2.0"</div>
                <div class="text-white">3# "proto" =&gt; (integer) 3</div>
                <div class="text-white">...</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Pipeline Support -->
    <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Pipelining</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-400">Clients can send many commands without waiting for each reply. SoliKV decodes the whole pipeline, runs consecutive commands that land on the same shard under one lock hold, and writes the replies in one buffer. Measured numbers are on the <a href="/docs/benchmarks" class="text-indigo-400 hover:text-white">benchmarks</a> page.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Client Compatibility -->
    <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Client Compatibility</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-400 mb-4">Standard clients work, including their cluster modes: <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">CLUSTER SLOTS</code>, <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">CLUSTER SHARDS</code> and <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">COMMAND</code> reply in Redis 7's format. <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">INFO</code> reports <code class="text-indigo-400 bg-indigo-500/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">redis_version:7.2.0</code> for clients that check it.</p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-4">
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 text-center text-sm">redis-cli (incl. <span class="font-mono">--cluster</span>)</div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 text-center text-sm">redis-py</div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 text-center text-sm">ioredis (Node.js)</div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 text-center text-sm">go-redis (Go)</div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 text-center text-sm">Jedis / Lettuce (Java)</div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/10 text-center text-sm">redis-rs (Rust)</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
